# 📡 Wireshark Traffic Analysis Demo

▶️Full Walkthrough: https://youtu.be/Twgs1CZ13V0

## 🎯 Objective

Demonstrate the use of Wireshark to capture and analyze network traffic, identify protocols, and detect potentially suspicious activity.

---

## 🧰 Tools Used

- Wireshark  
- Kali Linux / Windows  
- Test environment (lab traffic / pcap file)  

---

## 🖥️ Lab Environment

- Host Machine: Kali Linux / Windows  
- Network: Local lab environment  
- Traffic Source: Simulated browsing/test pcap file  

---

## 📦 Capture Overview

Captured live network traffic to analyze communication between devices and identify protocols and patterns.

## 🔍 Key Findings

- Identified DNS queries resolving external domains  
- Observed HTTP traffic in plaintext  
- Reconstructed full TCP sessions  

## 🧠 Key Takeaways

- Network traffic can reveal sensitive information if not encrypted  
- Packet filtering is essential for efficient analysis  
- Following streams helps reconstruct communication  
- Monitoring unusual ports can indicate suspicious activity 

